  "atlasSkullBlurb": "القحف والفك السفلي معًا",
  "@atlasSkullBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Cranium and mandible together (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasSkullSummary": "الرأس العظمي كاملًا: القحف مع الفك السفلي. اثنان وعشرون عظمًا في المجموع، تربطها دروز متشابكة؛ ولا يتحرك بحرية سوى الفك السفلي.",
  "@atlasSkullSummary": {
    "description": "English: The complete bony head: the cranium together with the mandible. Twenty-two bones in all, joined by interlocking sutures; only the mandible articulates freely. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasSkullLm1": "الدروز الإكليلي والسهمي واللامي",
  "@atlasSkullLm1": {
    "description": "English: Coronal, sagittal and lambdoid sutures (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasSkullLm2": "محجرا العينين والفتحة الكمثرية (الأنفية)",
  "@atlasSkullLm2": {
    "description": "English: Orbits and the piriform (nasal) aperture (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasSkullLm3": "الثقبة العظمى في قاعدة الجمجمة",
  "@atlasSkullLm3": {
    "description": "English: Foramen magnum on the basicranium (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasSkullLm4": "الناتئان الخشائيان خلف قناتي الأذن",
  "@atlasSkullLm4": {
    "description": "English: Mastoid processes behind the ear canals (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasSkullSiding": "متناظرة. يُعرف الاتجاه من العظم الجبهي (في الأمام) وحرشفة العظم القذالي (في الخلف).",
  "@atlasSkullSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical. Orientation comes from the frontal bone (anterior) and the occipital squama (posterior). (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumBlurb": "الجمجمة من دون فكها",
  "@atlasCraniumBlurb": {
    "description": "English: The skull without its jaw (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumSummary": "الجمجمة بعد إزالة الفك السفلي. تحيط بالدماغ وتحميه؛ وتتكوّن القبة من العظام الجبهي والجداري والصدغي والقذالي.",
  "@atlasCraniumSummary": {
    "description": "English: The skull with the mandible removed. Encloses and protects the brain; the vault is made of frontal, parietal, temporal and occipital bones. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumLm1": "الحافتان فوق الحجاجين — أبرز في جماجم الذكور",
  "@atlasCraniumLm1": {
    "description": "English: Supraorbital ridges — heavier in male crania (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumLm2": "الخطوط القفوية على العظم القذالي",
  "@atlasCraniumLm2": {
    "description": "English: Nuchal lines on the occipital (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumLm3": "الخطوط الصدغية الممتدة عبر العظمين الجداريين",
  "@atlasCraniumLm3": {
    "description": "English: Temporal lines sweeping across the parietals (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumLm4": "الصماخ السمعي الظاهر",
  "@atlasCraniumLm4": {
    "description": "English: External auditory meatus (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumSiding": "متناظرة حين تكون كاملة. تُحدَّد جهة قطع القبة المنفردة من اتجاه الدروز ونمط أخاديد الأوعية السحائية.",
  "@atlasCraniumSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical when complete. Isolated vault fragments are sided by suture direction and meningeal groove patterning. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasCraniumAka": "القلنسوة (القبة فقط)",
  "@atlasCraniumAka": {
    "description": "English: Calvarium (vault only) (Atlas: another name for this bone)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleBlurb": "الفك السفلي؛ كثيف ومتين",
  "@atlasMandibleBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Lower jaw; dense and durable (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleSummary": "الفك السفلي — العظم الوحيد المتحرك بحرية في الجمجمة. كثيف ومتماسك، لذا يصمد أمام الدفن والحرق أكثر من معظم العظام.",
  "@atlasMandibleSummary": {
    "description": "English: The lower jaw — the only freely mobile bone of the skull. Dense and compact, so it survives burial and burning better than most. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleLm1": "البروز الذقني (الذقن)",
  "@atlasMandibleLm1": {
    "description": "English: Mental protuberance (the chin) (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleLm2": "زاوية الفك حيث يلتقي الفرع بالجسم",
  "@atlasMandibleLm2": {
    "description": "English: Gonial angle where ramus meets body (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleLm3": "لقمة الفك والناتئ الإكليلي",
  "@atlasMandibleLm3": {
    "description": "English: Mandibular condyle and coronoid process (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleLm4": "الثقبة الذقنية أسفل الضواحك",
  "@atlasMandibleLm4": {
    "description": "English: Mental foramen below the premolars (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasMandibleSiding": "متناظر حين يكون كاملًا. يُحدَّد جانب نصف الفك من اتجاه صعود الفرع ومن جهة انحناء صف الأسنان.",
  "@atlasMandibleSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical when whole. A half-mandible is sided by the direction the ramus rises and by which way the tooth row curves. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasFemurBlurb": "عظم الفخذ؛ أفضل مؤشر على طول القامة",
  "@atlasFemurBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Thigh bone; best stature indicator (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasFemurSummary": "عظم الفخذ — أطول عظام الجسم وأقواها. طوله الأقصى هو الأوثق ارتباطًا بطول القامة في الحياة.",
  "@atlasFemurSummary": {
    "description": "English: The thigh bone — the longest and strongest bone in the body. Its maximum length carries the tightest correlation with living stature. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasFemurLm1": "رأس كروي فيه نُقرة الرأس",
  "@atlasFemurLm1": {
    "description": "English: Spherical head with the fovea capitis (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasFemurLm2": "المدوّران الكبير والصغير",
  "@atlasFemurLm2": {
    "description": "English: Greater and lesser trochanters (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasFemurLm3": "الخط الخشن على الوجه الخلفي لجسم العظم",
  "@atlasFemurLm3": {
    "description": "English: Linea aspera ridging the posterior shaft (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasFemurLm4": "اللقمتان الإنسية والوحشية عند الركبة",
  "@atlasFemurLm4": {
    "description": "English: Medial and lateral condyles at the knee (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasFemurSiding": "أمسك العظم عموديًا: يتجه الرأس نحو الداخل ويكون الخط الخشن إلى الخلف. الجهة التي يشير إليها الرأس هي جهة الجسم.",
  "@atlasFemurSiding": {
    "description": "English: Hold the bone upright: the head points medially and the linea aspera faces posteriorly. The side the head points to is the side of the body. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaBlurb": "عظم الساق؛ جسم مثلث المقطع",
  "@atlasTibiaBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Shin bone; triangular shaft (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaSummary": "عظم القصبة، الإنسي والحامل للوزن في أسفل الساق. جسمه المثلث المقطع مميز حتى في القطع المكسورة.",
  "@atlasTibiaSummary": {
    "description": "English: The shin bone, medial and weight-bearing in the lower leg. Its triangular shaft is distinctive even in fragments. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaLm1": "الحدبة الظنبوبية في مقدمة الجزء العلوي من الجسم",
  "@atlasTibiaLm1": {
    "description": "English: Tibial tuberosity on the anterior proximal shaft (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaLm2": "حافة أمامية حادة",
  "@atlasTibiaLm2": {
    "description": "English: Sharp anterior crest (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaLm3": "الكعب الإنسي عند الكاحل",
  "@atlasTibiaLm3": {
    "description": "English: Medial malleolus at the ankle (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaLm4": "لقمتان إنسية ووحشية مسطحتان",
  "@atlasTibiaLm4": {
    "description": "English: Flat medial and lateral condyles (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTibiaSiding": "يبرز الكعب الإنسي في الجهة نفسها من الجسم التي جاء منها العظم؛ وتحدد الحدبة الظنبوبية الجهة الأمامية.",
  "@atlasTibiaSiding": {
    "description": "English: The medial malleolus projects on the same side as the body it came from; the tibial tuberosity marks the front. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusBlurb": "أعلى الذراع، من الكتف إلى المرفق",
  "@atlasHumerusBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Upper arm, shoulder to elbow (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusSummary": "عظم أعلى الذراع، يمتد من مفصل الكتف إلى المرفق. لا يفوقه طولًا إلا عظم الفخذ.",
  "@atlasHumerusSummary": {
    "description": "English: The upper arm bone, running from the shoulder joint to the elbow. Second only to the femur in length. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusLm1": "رأس مستدير مع الحديبتين الكبرى والصغرى",
  "@atlasHumerusLm1": {
    "description": "English: Rounded head with greater and lesser tubercles (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusLm2": "الحدبة الدالية في منتصف الجسم",
  "@atlasHumerusLm2": {
    "description": "English: Deltoid tuberosity mid-shaft (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusLm3": "الحفرة الزُّجّية في الخلف عند الطرف البعيد",
  "@atlasHumerusLm3": {
    "description": "English: Olecranon fossa on the posterior distal end (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusLm4": "البكرة والرُّؤيس تشكّلان مفصل المرفق",
  "@atlasHumerusLm4": {
    "description": "English: Trochlea and capitulum forming the elbow (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasHumerusSiding": "أوقفه عموديًا ورأسه مواجه لك: تقع الحفرة الزجية في الخلف، ويتجه الرأس نحو الداخل باتجاه خط منتصف الجسم.",
  "@atlasHumerusSiding": {
    "description": "English: Stand it upright with the head facing you: the olecranon fossa sits posteriorly, and the head turns medially toward the body midline. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusBlurb": "العظم الوحشي في الساعد، في جهة الإبهام",
  "@atlasRadiusBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Lateral forearm, on the thumb side (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusSummary": "عظم الساعد الوحشي، في جهة الإبهام. يدور فوق الزند ليقلب راحة اليد.",
  "@atlasRadiusSummary": {
    "description": "English: The lateral forearm bone, on the thumb side. It rotates over the ulna to turn the palm. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusLm1": "رأس قرصي الشكل في الطرف القريب",
  "@atlasRadiusLm1": {
    "description": "English: Disc-shaped proximal head (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusLm2": "الحدبة الكعبرية أسفل العنق مباشرة",
  "@atlasRadiusLm2": {
    "description": "English: Radial tuberosity just below the neck (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusLm3": "طرف بعيد عريض ومتسع",
  "@atlasRadiusLm3": {
    "description": "English: Broad, flared distal end (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusLm4": "الناتئ الإبري عند الرسغ",
  "@atlasRadiusLm4": {
    "description": "English: Styloid process at the wrist (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRadiusSiding": "الرأس الصغير في الطرف القريب والطرف العريض في الطرف البعيد؛ ويتجه الناتئ الإبري نحو الخارج، بعيدًا عن خط المنتصف.",
  "@atlasRadiusSiding": {
    "description": "English: The small head is proximal and the broad end distal; the styloid process points laterally, away from the midline. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaBlurb": "العظم الإنسي في الساعد؛ رأس المرفق",
  "@atlasUlnaBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Medial forearm; point of the elbow (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaSummary": "عظم الساعد الإنسي، في جهة الخنصر. يشكّل مفصل المرفق الرزّي، وهو الشريك الثابت الذي تدور حوله الكعبرة.",
  "@atlasUlnaSummary": {
    "description": "English: The medial forearm bone, on the little-finger side. Forms the hinge of the elbow and is the stable partner the radius rotates around. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaLm1": "الناتئ الزُّجّي — رأس المرفق",
  "@atlasUlnaLm1": {
    "description": "English: Olecranon process — the point of the elbow (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaLm2": "الثلمة البكرية التي تمسك بعظم العضد",
  "@atlasUlnaLm2": {
    "description": "English: Trochlear notch gripping the humerus (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaLm3": "الناتئ المنقاري أسفل الثلمة",
  "@atlasUlnaLm3": {
    "description": "English: Coronoid process below the notch (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaLm4": "رأس بعيد نحيل مع ناتئ إبري",
  "@atlasUlnaLm4": {
    "description": "English: Slender distal head with styloid process (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasUlnaSiding": "تنفتح الثلمة البكرية نحو الأمام؛ وحين يكون الزُّج في الأعلى والثلمة مواجهة لك، ينحني جسم العظم نحو جهة الجسم.",
  "@atlasUlnaSiding": {
    "description": "English: The trochlear notch opens anteriorly; with the olecranon up and the notch facing you, the shaft curves toward the body side. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaBlurb": "لوح الكتف؛ صفيحة رقيقة مثلثة",
  "@atlasScapulaBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Shoulder blade; thin triangular plate (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaSummary": "لوح الكتف — صفيحة مثلثة رقيقة تستقر على ظهر القفص الصدري. رقيقة لدرجة أنها كثيرًا ما تبقى على شكل قطع فقط.",
  "@atlasScapulaSummary": {
    "description": "English: The shoulder blade — a thin triangular plate riding on the back of the ribcage. Thin enough that the blade often survives only as fragments. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaLm1": "الشوكة الممتدة عبر السطح الخلفي",
  "@atlasScapulaLm1": {
    "description": "English: Spine running across the posterior surface (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaLm2": "الناتئ الأخرمي عند طرف الكتف",
  "@atlasScapulaLm2": {
    "description": "English: Acromion process at the shoulder tip (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaLm3": "الناتئ الغرابي المعقوف في الأمام",
  "@atlasScapulaLm3": {
    "description": "English: Hooked coracoid process anteriorly (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaLm4": "الحفرة العنابية التي يستقر فيها رأس العضد",
  "@atlasScapulaLm4": {
    "description": "English: Glenoid fossa receiving the humeral head (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasScapulaSiding": "تتجه الحفرة العنابية نحو الخارج وتقع الشوكة على السطح الخلفي؛ والجهة التي تواجهها الحفرة هي جهة الجسم.",
  "@atlasScapulaSiding": {
    "description": "English: The glenoid fossa faces laterally and the spine sits on the posterior surface; the side the fossa faces is the side of the body. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaBlurb": "عظم الورك؛ أفضل مؤشر على الجنس",
  "@atlasOsCoxaBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Hip bone; best indicator of sex (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaSummary": "عظم الورك: الحرقفة والإسك والعانة ملتحمة عند الحُق. أوثق عظم منفرد لتقدير الجنس وعمر البالغين.",
  "@atlasOsCoxaSummary": {
    "description": "English: The hip bone: ilium, ischium and pubis fused at the acetabulum. The single most reliable element for estimating sex and adult age. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaLm1": "الثلمة الوركية الكبرى — عريضة عند الإناث وضيقة عند الذكور",
  "@atlasOsCoxaLm1": {
    "description": "English: Greater sciatic notch — broad in females, narrow in males (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaLm2": "الزاوية تحت العانة والقوس البطني",
  "@atlasOsCoxaLm2": {
    "description": "English: Subpubic angle and the ventral arc (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaLm3": "السطح الأذيني، يُستخدم لتقدير العمر عند الوفاة",
  "@atlasOsCoxaLm3": {
    "description": "English: Auricular surface, used for age-at-death (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaLm4": "الحُق الذي يستقر فيه رأس الفخذ",
  "@atlasOsCoxaLm4": {
    "description": "English: Acetabulum receiving the femoral head (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaSiding": "وجّه جناح الحرقفة إلى الأعلى والحُق إلى الخارج: تقع العانة في الأمام وتنفتح الثلمة الوركية نحو الخلف.",
  "@atlasOsCoxaSiding": {
    "description": "English: Point the iliac blade up and the acetabulum out: the pubis sits anteriorly and the sciatic notch opens posteriorly. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasOsCoxaAka": "العظم الغُفل، عظم الورك",
  "@atlasOsCoxaAka": {
    "description": "English: Innominate, hip bone (Atlas: another name for this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Blurb": "ضلوع غير نموذجية؛ مسطحة وشديدة الانحناء",
  "@atlasRib12Blurb": {
    "description": "English: Atypical ribs; flat and sharply curved (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Summary": "الضلعان الأولان غير نموذجيين. الضلع 1 هو الأقصر والأعرض والأشد انحناءً؛ والضلع 2 أطول لكنه يحتفظ بالشكل المسطح نفسه.",
  "@atlasRib12Summary": {
    "description": "English: The first two ribs are atypical. Rib 1 is the shortest, broadest and most sharply curved; rib 2 is longer but keeps the same flattened set. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Lm1": "الضلع 1 مسطح، له سطح علوي وسطح سفلي",
  "@atlasRib12Lm1": {
    "description": "English: Rib 1 lies flat, with superior and inferior surfaces (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Lm2": "الحديبة الأخمعية مع أخاديد للأوعية تحت الترقوة",
  "@atlasRib12Lm2": {
    "description": "English: Scalene tubercle with grooves for the subclavian vessels (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Lm3": "يحمل الضلع 2 حدبة للعضلة المنشارية الأمامية",
  "@atlasRib12Lm3": {
    "description": "English: Rib 2 carries a tuberosity for serratus anterior (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Lm4": "وجيه مفصلي واحد على رأس الضلع 1",
  "@atlasRib12Lm4": {
    "description": "English: Single articular facet on the head of rib 1 (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib12Siding": "ضع الضلع مسطحًا ورأسه إلى الخلف: يتجه السطح الداخلي المقعّر نحو خط المنتصف، فيدلّ على الجهة.",
  "@atlasRib12Siding": {
    "description": "English: Lay the rib flat with the head backward: the concave inner surface faces the midline, giving the side. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibBlurb": "الضلوع 3–9؛ رأس وحديبة وأخدود ضلعي",
  "@atlasTypicalRibBlurb": {
    "description": "English: Ribs 3–9; head, tubercle, costal groove (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibSummary": "تشترك الضلوع من 3 إلى 9 في تصميم واحد: رأس وعنق وحديبة وجسم طويل منحنٍ يلتوي عند الزاوية.",
  "@atlasTypicalRibSummary": {
    "description": "English: Ribs 3 through 9 share one plan: a head, neck, tubercle and a long curving body that twists at the angle. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibLm1": "نصفا وجيه مفصلي على الرأس",
  "@atlasTypicalRibLm1": {
    "description": "English: Two demifacets on the head (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibLm2": "حديبة تتمفصل مع ناتئ مستعرض",
  "@atlasTypicalRibLm2": {
    "description": "English: Tubercle articulating with a transverse process (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibLm3": "زاوية يتغير عندها اتجاه جسم الضلع",
  "@atlasTypicalRibLm3": {
    "description": "English: Angle where the shaft changes direction (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibLm4": "الأخدود الضلعي على امتداد الحافة السفلية الداخلية",
  "@atlasTypicalRibLm4": {
    "description": "English: Costal groove along the inner inferior border (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasTypicalRibSiding": "يمتد الأخدود الضلعي على الحافة السفلية الداخلية؛ وحين يكون الأخدود في الأسفل والداخل، يشير الرأس إلى الخلف ويدلّ على الجهة.",
  "@atlasTypicalRibSiding": {
    "description": "English: The costal groove runs on the internal inferior edge; with the groove down and inside, the head points to the back and gives the side. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Blurb": "الضلوع العائمة؛ قصيرة وغير متصلة",
  "@atlasRib1112Blurb": {
    "description": "English: Floating ribs; short and unattached (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Summary": "الضلوع العائمة. قصيرة ومستدقة وغير متصلة من الأمام، ولهذا تفتقر إلى معظم ملامح الضلع النموذجي.",
  "@atlasRib1112Summary": {
    "description": "English: The floating ribs. Short, tapering and unattached at the front, which is why they lack most of the features a typical rib carries. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Lm1": "وجيه مفصلي واحد على الرأس",
  "@atlasRib1112Lm1": {
    "description": "English: Single articular facet on the head (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Lm2": "لا عنق ولا حديبة",
  "@atlasRib1112Lm2": {
    "description": "English: No neck and no tubercle (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Lm3": "أخدود ضلعي ضعيف أو معدوم",
  "@atlasRib1112Lm3": {
    "description": "English: Little or no costal groove (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Lm4": "طرف أمامي مدبب ينتهي بغضروف",
  "@atlasRib1112Lm4": {
    "description": "English: Pointed, cartilage-tipped anterior end (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasRib1112Siding": "الانحناء وحده يدلّ على الجهة: يتجه السطح المقعّر نحو خط المنتصف.",
  "@atlasRib1112Siding": {
    "description": "English: Curvature alone gives the side: the concave surface faces the midline. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalBlurb": "C1–C7؛ الوحيدة ذات الثقوب المستعرضة",
  "@atlasCervicalBlurb": {
    "description": "English: C1–C7; the only ones with transverse foramina (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalSummary": "فقرات الرقبة السبع، C1–C7. أصغر أجسام في العمود الفقري، والفقرات الوحيدة التي في نواتئها المستعرضة ثقوب.",
  "@atlasCervicalSummary": {
    "description": "English: The seven neck vertebrae, C1–C7. Smallest bodies in the column and the only vertebrae with holes in the transverse processes. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalLm1": "الثقوب المستعرضة — علامة مميزة لهذه المنطقة",
  "@atlasCervicalLm1": {
    "description": "English: Transverse foramina — diagnostic for the region (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalLm2": "ليس للفقرة C1 (الفهقة) جسم؛ وتحمل C2 (المحور) الناتئ السني",
  "@atlasCervicalLm2": {
    "description": "English: C1 (atlas) has no body; C2 (axis) carries the dens (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalLm3": "نواتئ شوكية مشقوقة في C2–C6",
  "@atlasCervicalLm3": {
    "description": "English: Bifid spinous processes on C2–C6 (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalLm4": "ثقبة فقرية كبيرة مثلثة",
  "@atlasCervicalLm4": {
    "description": "English: Large triangular vertebral foramen (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasCervicalSiding": "متناظرة. يُعرف موقعها في السلسلة من الناتئ الشوكي وحجم الجسم؛ وللفقرة C7 شوكة طويلة غير مشقوقة تُعرف بـ«البارزة».",
  "@atlasCervicalSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical. Position in the series is read from the spinous process and body size; C7 has the long, unsplit \"prominens\" spine. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicBlurb": "T1–T12؛ تحمل الوجيهات الضلعية",
  "@atlasThoracicBlurb": {
    "description": "English: T1–T12; carry the costal facets (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicSummary": "فقرات أعلى الظهر الاثنتا عشرة، T1–T12. تتمفصل كل واحدة مع زوج من الضلوع، والوجيهات الخاصة بتلك الضلوع تميّز هذه المنطقة.",
  "@atlasThoracicSummary": {
    "description": "English: The twelve vertebrae of the upper back, T1–T12. Each one articulates with a pair of ribs, and the facets for those ribs identify the region. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicLm1": "وجيهات ضلعية على الجسم والنواتئ المستعرضة",
  "@atlasThoracicLm1": {
    "description": "English: Costal facets on the body and transverse processes (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicLm2": "أجسام فقرية على شكل قلب",
  "@atlasThoracicLm2": {
    "description": "English: Heart-shaped vertebral bodies (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicLm3": "نواتئ شوكية طويلة مائلة بشدة نحو الأسفل",
  "@atlasThoracicLm3": {
    "description": "English: Long spinous processes angled steeply downward (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicLm4": "ثقبة فقرية دائرية",
  "@atlasThoracicLm4": {
    "description": "English: Circular vertebral foramen (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasThoracicSiding": "متناظرة. يُستدل على الترتيب من حجم الجسم ومن مدى تراكب الناتئ الشوكي على الفقرة التي تحته.",
  "@atlasThoracicSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical. Sequence is judged from body size and how far the spinous process overlaps the vertebra below. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarBlurb": "L1–L5؛ الأثقل في العمود الفقري",
  "@atlasLumbarBlurb": {
    "description": "English: L1–L5; the heaviest in the column (Atlas: one line under the bone name in the list)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarSummary": "فقرات أسفل الظهر الخمس، L1–L5. الأكبر والأمتن في العمود الفقري، مصممة لتحمّل الوزن لا للحركة.",
  "@atlasLumbarSummary": {
    "description": "English: The five vertebrae of the lower back, L1–L5. The largest and most robust in the column, built for load rather than movement. (Atlas, anatomy text for experts. Keep the Latin terms where your language uses them)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarLm1": "أجسام ضخمة على شكل كلية",
  "@atlasLumbarLm1": {
    "description": "English: Massive kidney-shaped bodies (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarLm2": "لا ثقوب مستعرضة ولا وجيهات ضلعية",
  "@atlasLumbarLm2": {
    "description": "English: No transverse foramina and no costal facets (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarLm3": "نواتئ شوكية قصيرة كليلة على شكل فأس",
  "@atlasLumbarLm3": {
    "description": "English: Short, blunt, hatchet-shaped spinous processes (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarLm4": "نواتئ حلمية على الوجيهات المفصلية العلوية",
  "@atlasLumbarLm4": {
    "description": "English: Mammillary processes on the superior articular facets (Atlas: one thing an expert looks for on this bone)"
  },
  "atlasLumbarSiding": "متناظرة. تُعرف الفقرة L5 بشكلها الإسفيني، فهي أعمق من الأمام منها من الخلف، حيث تلتقي بالعجز.",
  "@atlasLumbarSiding": {
    "description": "English: Symmetrical. L5 is recognised by its wedge shape, deeper in front than behind, where it meets the sacrum. (Atlas: how to tell left from right, or the place in a series)"
  },
  "phaseDoc1Title": "هل يوجد عظم؟",
  "@phaseDoc1Title": {
    "description": "English: Is there a bone? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc1Detail": "يتحقق Ossia أولًا من وجود عظم في الصورة أصلًا، حتى لا يحصل غصن أو حجر على إجابة مختلَقة.",
  "@phaseDoc1Detail": {
    "description": "English: First Ossia checks there's a bone in the photo at all, so a stick or a stone doesn't get a made-up answer. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc2Title": "إنسان أم حيوان؟",
  "@phaseDoc2Title": {
    "description": "English: Human or animal? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc2Detail": "ثم يقرر إن كان العظم من إنسان أم من حيوان. كل ما يلي يعتمد على هذه الخطوة.",
  "@phaseDoc2Detail": {
    "description": "English: Next it decides whether the bone came from a person or an animal. Everything after depends on this step. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc3Title": "أي عظم؟",
  "@phaseDoc3Title": {
    "description": "English: Which bone? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc3Detail": "ستة عشر نوعًا من العظام، من الجمجمة والفك إلى الضلوع والعمود الفقري والورك والأطراف. ترى أفضل ثلاثة تخمينات، لا الفائز وحده.",
  "@phaseDoc3Detail": {
    "description": "English: Sixteen kinds of bone, from the skull and jaw to the ribs, spine, hip and limbs. You see its top three guesses, not just the winner. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc4Title": "أي جزء؟",
  "@phaseDoc4Title": {
    "description": "English: Which part? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc4Detail": "هل تُظهر الصورة العظم كاملًا، أم وسطه (جسم العظم)، أم أحد طرفيه، أم قطعة مكسورة.",
  "@phaseDoc4Detail": {
    "description": "English: Whether the photo shows the whole bone, its middle (the shaft), one end, or a broken piece. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc5Title": "كامل أم مكسور؟",
  "@phaseDoc5Title": {
    "description": "English: Whole or broken? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc5Detail": "نعم أو لا بسرعة: هل العظم كامل، أم مجرد قطعة منه؟",
  "@phaseDoc5Detail": {
    "description": "English: A quick yes or no: is the bone complete, or only a fragment? (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc6Title": "الآثار والأضرار",
  "@phaseDoc6Title": {
    "description": "English: Marks and damage (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc6Detail": "يُفحص كل من الكسور وآثار القطع والحرق على حدة، لذا قد يُظهر عظم واحد الثلاثة معًا.",
  "@phaseDoc6Detail": {
    "description": "English: Breaks, cut marks and burning are each checked on their own, so one bone can show all three. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc7Title": "أي حيوان؟",
  "@phaseDoc7Title": {
    "description": "English: Which animal? (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc7Detail": "لعظام الحيوانات: ثديي أو طائر أو زاحف. وللثدييات أيضًا الفصيلة، مثل فصيلة الكلاب أو الأيائل أو البقر أو الخنازير أو القطط أو الدببة أو الأرانب أو الراكون أو الخيل، أو القوارض. ولا تُسمّى الفصيلة إلا حين يستطيع العظم إظهارها، كالجمجمة أو الفك أو عظم ساق كامل.",
  "@phaseDoc7Detail": {
    "description": "English: For animal bones: mammal, bird or reptile. For mammals, also the family, like the dog, deer, cattle, pig, cat, bear, rabbit, raccoon or horse family, or a rodent. The family is only named when the bone can show it, such as a skull, a jaw or a whole leg bone. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc8Title": "العمر والجنس",
  "@phaseDoc8Title": {
    "description": "English: Age and sex (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc8Detail": "للعظام البشرية فقط. اعتبرها تلميحًا يجب التحقق منه، لا إجابة قائمة بذاتها.",
  "@phaseDoc8Detail": {
    "description": "English: For human bones only. Treat these as a hint to check, never as an answer on their own. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
  "phaseDoc9Title": "جمع النتائج",
  "@phaseDoc9Title": {
    "description": "English: Putting it together (How analysis works: step title)"
  },
  "phaseDoc9Detail": "تُقرأ صور العظم نفسه من جهات مختلفة معًا، ويُقارن الطول الذي قسته بالحجم المعتاد لهذا العظم. وكلاهما يساعد حين تكون صورة واحدة غير واضحة.",
  "@phaseDoc9Detail": {
    "description": "English: Photos of the same bone from different sides are read together, and the length you measured is checked against the bone's usual size. Both help when one photo alone is unclear. (How analysis works: what this step does)"
  },
